{"type":"assistant.message","data":{"messageId":"fdefc120-bae5-4080-b5a0-454659fbb9f6","content":"Found it — the narrow-viewport media query flattens the tilt with plain `.gs-started__flipper` selectors, but the `:dir(rtl)` tilt rules earlier in the file have higher specificity (`:dir(rtl) .gs-started__flipper`), so they still win in RTL even inside the media query, leaving the rotateY tilt applied. ","toolRequests":[{"toolCallId":"toolu_013gQo2QsKX25Vn2u8VMmjcv","name":"replace_string_in_file","arguments":"{\"filePath\": \"/Users/dwahl/Scripts/pantoken/docs/.vitepress/theme/components/GetStartedTabs.vue\", \"oldString\": \"  .gs-started__stage.-agent .gs-started__flipper,\\n  .gs-started__stage.-agent::after {\\n    transform: rotateY(180deg);\\n  }\\n}\\n\", \"newString\": \"  .gs-started__stage.-agent .gs-started__flipper,\\n  .gs-started__stage.-agent::after {\\n    transform: rotateY(180deg);\\n  }\\n\\n  /* The `:dir(rtl)` tilt rules above outrank these plain selectors on specificity alone, so RTL\\n     needs its own flattening here or the tilt survives into the narrow layout. */\\n  :dir(rtl) .gs-started__flipper,\\n  :dir(rtl) .gs-started__stage::after {\\n    transform: rotateY(0deg);\\n  }\\n\\n  :dir(rtl) .gs-started__stage.-agent .gs-started__flipper,\\n  :dir(rtl) .gs-started__stage.-agent::after {\\n    transform: rotateY(180deg);\\n  }\\n}\\n\"}","type":"function"}],"reasoningText":"I'm noticing the narrow-viewport media query resets the flipper's rotation without being scoped to RTL, and since it's defined later in the file it likely overrides the earlier `:dir(rtl)` rule due to source order rather than specificity.\n\nActually comparing specificity more carefully, the `:dir(rtl) .gs-started__flipper` selector has two components (pseudo-class plus class), giving it higher specificity than the plain `.gs-started__flipper` used inside the media query. That means the RTL rule always wins regardless of order, so on narrow viewports in RTL the tilt never resets to 0deg as intended — this is the actual bug.\n\nAdding dir(rtl) overrides inside the narrow media block to flatten the tilt...\n\n"},"id":"2292c215-7872-4e4f-a525-c81960728c2e","timestamp":"2026-09-13T21:50:50.726Z","parentId":"2a7d6fdd-8c1a-4de1-ac24-c27728ff3905"}
